{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And they recounted to him, etc.</b> There is a fine point to examine in his saying <b>to him</b> — that they directed their speech specifically to him alone. But the statement was not to Moses alone but to the entire congregation who were listening, and it is written <b>and they said</b>, and it does not say 'to him.'" "<b>We came to the land, etc.</b> The meaning is that they arrived there safely and no mishap befell them, and they concluded by saying the phrase <b>to which you sent us</b> — meaning, because we fulfilled the mitzvah of your commission, we were protected. Or it may intend to say that because he provided them with an escort — namely, the one he sent with them — that is what stood by them to come to the land in peace. And perhaps it is for this reason that the verse was precise in saying <b>and they recounted to him</b> — to say that they related a matter pertaining to the greatness of Moses, for his merit stood by them. And its saying <b>and they said</b> is the report about the land, which pertains to the totality of Israel; therefore it does not say 'to him.'" "<b>And it also flows with milk and honey, etc.</b> They said 'and also' — because there had already preceded an expression of gratitude for the good measure, that a miracle was performed for them in their journey; they now add to give thanks also for the goodness of the land, that it flows with milk and honey, etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:32.663086840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}